{title: Everlasting Mercy}
{subtitle: Psalms 103:17–18}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] | [Bb] [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He knows how we are formed
He remem[F]bers that we are [C]dust
Our [Bb]days are like grass
[Dm]Blooming like a flower
The [Bb]wind passes over it
And it is gone
Its [Gm]place [A]knows it no [Dm]more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But the [Bb]steadfast [C]love of the [Dm]LORD
Rests from everlast[F]ing to ever[C]lasting
On [Gm]those who [A7]fear him
[Dm]And his righteous[C6]ness [Bb]too
On [C]their chil[Dm]dren's children
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
To those who keep his [C]covenant
And re[Dm]member to obey his precepts
[F]The LORD has established his [C]throne
In the [Gm]heavens high
His [Dm]kingdom rules over all
[Bb]With [C]power and [Dm]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But the [Bb]steadfast [C]love of the [Dm]LORD
Rests from everlast[F]ing to ever[C]lasting
On [Gm]those who [A7]fear him
[Dm]And his [C]righteousness [Bb]too
On their [C]children's [Dm]children
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Bless the [C]LORD you his an[Dm]gels
You [Bb]mighty ones who [C]do his [Dm]word
O[Bb]beying the [C]voice of his [Dm]word [C6][Bb][Am][Gm]
Bless the [Bb]LORD all his hosts
You his servants who [C]do his [Dm]will
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But the [Bb]steadfast [C]love of the [Dm]LORD
Rests from everlast[F]ing to ever[C]lasting
On [Gm]those who [Am]fear him
[Dm]And his [C]righteousness [Bb]too
On their [C]children's [Dm]children
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Ever[C]lasting love re[Bb]mains
From [C]age to [Dm]age
{end_of_verse}

